      "rationale": "L1 and L2 explicitly state the myc-tag was placed 'directly downstream of the putative signal peptide', which by the topology landmarks corresponds to insert_after_residue=23 (the last SP residue, P23), placing the tag before R24 (first mature extracellular residue). Python confirmed P at position 23 and R at position 24. The site is 120 residues from TM1, fully extracellular, and the cAMP assay in L2 demonstrates preserved GLP-1 potency, satisfying surface_and_function. Convergent evidence from SNAP-tag CRISPR knock-in (L12), SNAP-tag stable lines (L10, L11), and GFP fusion (L4, L5) all at the same junction further corroborates high confidence. mycGLP-1R: full-length, membrane-anchored human GLP-1R with a myc-tag inserted immediately downstream of the signal peptide (after residue 23, the last SP residue), expressed in HEK293 cells. The mature extracellular N-terminus begins at R24, 120 residues from TM1 (144). Multiple independent groups also placed SNAP-tags (L10, L11, L12) and GFP (L4, L5) at the same junction, all confirming surface display. [validation: surface_and_function; position: inferred; source: paper; cited_tag_residue: 23; entailment_verified: True]",
