  "literature_notes": "C-terminal tags (L3: YFP; L6/L7/L8: FLAG): the GLP-1R C-terminus falls within the intracellular span 406-463 and does not qualify as an extracellular site. ECL3 amber-codon/UAA sites (L9, H374/R376/G377/T378): H374 is the last residue of TM6 (349-374) and is not extracellular. R376, G377, and T378 lie in ECL3 (375-378), but ECL3 is only 4 residues long; Python confirmed that no position in this loop satisfies the >=3-residue buffer from both TM6 (ends 374) and TM7 (starts 379) simultaneously, and the modification reported (single unnatural amino acid incorporation via amber suppression for click-chemistry labeling) is a single-residue substitution rather than a 13-23 aa epitope-tag insertion \u2014 the loop could not accommodate such an insert. ICL3 cpGFP insertion (L13, between K336 and T343): the ICL3 span 326-348 is intracellular; excluded. L14 (FLAG at N-terminus of GLP1R ORF): the construct adds an HA secretion motif plus FLAG to the N-terminus of the full ORF; the position of the FLAG relative to the SP cleavage site is ambiguous and cannot be pinned \u2014 L1/L2 provide unambiguous evidence for the same mature N-terminal junction and are used instead.",
